sequenceDiagram
    actor Host as Unity Host Result Outbox
    participant C as MatchResultsController
    participant M as MatchResultService
    participant Q as MatchProfilePostProcessingService
    participant R as RewardService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    actor Player as Result UI / ResultRewardBridge

    Host->>C: PUT /api/matches/{matchId}/result (JWT)
    C->>M: SubmitAsync(hostId, matchId, request)
    M->>DB: Validate host lease, roster, match state, payload
    alt Invalid or conflicting result
        M-->>C: Rejected (reason-specific)
        C-->>Host: 4xx response
    else New or identical replay
        M->>DB: Commit match result if new; replay is idempotent
        DB-->>M: Accepted result
        M-->>C: IsReplay flag and result status
        C->>Q: EnqueueAsync(matchId) (LTP)
        Note over Q: Failure to queue is logged; accepted result retained.
        C->>R: ProcessAsync(matchId)
        R->>DB: Validate reward policy; grant wallet/XP atomically
        alt Reward committed or already complete
            DB-->>R: Completed / replay
            R-->>C: RewardStatus Completed
        else Reward processing failed
            R-->>C: Failure; reward remains Pending
        end
        C-->>Host: 201 new / 200 replay; reward may be Pending
    end

    Player->>C: GET /api/matches/{matchId}/reward/me (JWT)
    C->>R: GetForUserAsync(matchId, userId)
    R->>DB: Read completed reward grant and profile
    alt Reward confirmed
        R-->>C: RewardMeResponse
        C-->>Player: 200 OK; display confirmed amounts
    else Reward still pending
        R-->>C: RewardPending
        C-->>Player: 409 Conflict; show Pending
    else Missing or inconsistent records
        R-->>C: Reason-specific error
        C-->>Player: 4xx; do not claim reward
    end
    Note over Host,Player: HTTP calls use Unity API clients; controllers never call Unity components directly.
